# does not settle: S-63 -- the solve gate records the report and expects the stall until the defect closes.
# Layout ladder, step 8b (plan/20-core-domain/29-layout-ladder.md): the same two injection
# branches in series. The radiators come first and take 20 kW at 50/40 from the 60 C supply, which
# fixes the stream at 0.239 kg/s; the AHU then cools that stream from 40 to the 30 C return, so its
# duty is not stated -- it is the 10 kW the balance leaves -- and HS1 states the total 30 kW. Stating
# the AHU's duty too over-specifies a series circuit by one, and the solve ran non-finite. `N4`
# joins the radiators' return to the AHU's supply and has two connections, so it is inline (D-114).
# The solver does not converge on this series shape yet, whatever is stated (S-63); the layout does
# not need the solution and is drawn all the same.

fluidscript 1
project static plant_01

circuit heating 100
fluid water

HS1     heat_exchanger power=30 kW out=60

connections
N1 - HS1 - N3
N5 - N1

N1 node p=250

circuit radiators 102

HE_RAD  load in=50 out=40 power=20 kW
TV_RAD  three_way_valve
PU_RAD  pump
PR1     pipe length=18 dn=25
PR2     pipe length=18 dn=25

connections
N3 - PR1 - TV_RAD.a
NM_RAD - TV_RAD.b
TV_RAD.ab - PU_RAD - HE_RAD - NM_RAD
NM_RAD - PR2 - N4

circuit AHU 101

HE_AHU  load in=35 out=30
TV_AHU  three_way_valve
PU_AHU  pump
PA1     pipe length=12 dn=25
PA2     pipe length=12 dn=25

connections
N4 - PA1 - TV_AHU.a
NM_AHU - TV_AHU.b
TV_AHU.ab - PU_AHU - HE_AHU - NM_AHU
NM_AHU - PA2 - N5
